  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">One drop one hope: Drip Irrigation in Southern Angola</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project plans to implement drip irrigation systems in rural communities in Cunene, Huila and Namibe who rely on small scale farming and are constantly affected by seasonal draught in Angola. Through a study-based data collection, we will implement cost effetely, eco-friendly and efficient method of watering crops, providing more uniform, timely and precise application of water. The project involves constructing a network of drip irrigation tape which delivers water to the base of the plants, either on the soil surface or underneath, directly on the root zone. The outcome of this project is a more rapid growth and earlier harvest, higher quality crops at higher yields as well as cost saving associated with greatly reduced water usage in period of drought, especially this year with the impact of El Nino. Emphasis will be given to women and young girls who are household heads and have farming as a source for food security and living income for their families. The purpose of this project is to provide a sustainable and practical long-term solution to combat the impact of seasonal drought in the south of Angola on food security and farming.</narrative>
  </description>
